        <exercise id="_30e5ad0a-53bd-4e8c-8f59-ed1cdc37135d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(4x\;\leq\;8\)</para>
              <para>Select <emphasis>two</emphasis> properties that could be
              used to solve the inequality</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division
              Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--END
      ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <!--BEGIN
      ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->

        <exercise id="_9aca208b-a54e-4a20-b884-3a200c574adc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(–\frac12x\;\leq\;1\;\)</para>
            <para>Select <emphasis>two</emphasis> properties that could be used to solve the
              inequality</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division
              Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--END
      ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Is there anything unique about the method used to solve \(–\frac12x\leq1\)? Explain.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Yes. The inequality contains a less than or equal to symbol \((\leq)\). However, in
            the solution there is a greater than or equal to symbol \((\geq)\). When using the
            Multiplication and Division Properties of Inequality, you must reverse the symbol when
            you multiply or divide by a negative number.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->


    <section>
      <note class="self-check">
        <para>Solve the inequality. Which number line represents the solution?</para>
        <para>\(–\;\frac13m\;\leq\;5\)</para>
      </note>
